{#
  Renders <aside class="rail"> — the chapter nav sidebar. Matches the site's real markup and,
  critically, its EXISTING onclick="goChapter(id, trackId)" wiring exactly (index.html, root
  goChapter() implementation — unmodified, not reimplemented here). goChapter() toggles a
  .ch-active class (see public/css/main.css's .chapter/.chapter.ch-active rules) and defaults
  to activating the first .chapter in the DOM if none is active yet — so chapter render order
  in the parent template MUST match this rail's order exactly, which itself must match the
  `chapters` array's order (already true — content/{track}/*.json chapters render in array order).

  "Chapters"/"Practice set"/"Test generator"/"Downloads" are real, site-wide (not track-specific)
  dictionary strings, used identically on MOST tracks — embedded here via the bilingual macro with
  their real translations (not invented), rather than duplicated as per-track content data. A real
  exception exists (apbc, WP19): its rail link reads "Exam practice"/⊘, not "Practice set"/§ — use
  practiceSetLabel/practiceSetIcon (typically sourced from that track's practiceSet.heading/.icon,
  course_schema.json) to override per track; omit them to get the site-wide default.

  Expects: trackId, chapters (array, same objects rendered by chapter.njk — reads chapterNumber/
  railLabel/title/id), and the REAL section ids (NOT derived from trackId — must match each
  partial's own `sectionId` exactly, see downloads-block.njk/practice-set.njk/test-generator.njk):
  practiceSetId (optional — omit to hide the link), testGeneratorId (optional), downloadsId.
  Optional overrides: practiceSetLabel, practiceSetIcon.

  railExtra (optional, raw HTML string, WP24): appended as the LAST child inside <aside>, before
  the closing tag — real case: ibhl's real source has a "Curriculum Mapping" <select> widget
  (window.CSGamify.mapCurriculum) inside its rail, found on NO other track (not even ibsl, the
  other IB track) — genuinely track-exclusive, so it's passed as literal markup from the track's
  own index.njk rather than modeled as new schema fields for a one-instance feature.

  chapter.railGroupLabel (optional, WP33, calculus): when a chapter carries this, an extra
  <p class="rt" style="margin-top:16px">{label}</p> renders immediately before that chapter's own
  link — calculus's real rail splits into two labeled groups ("Chapters" / "Multivariable · Calc
  III"), a one-off not modeled as a general per-track grouping mechanism.

  railNoTrackId (optional boolean, WP33, calculus): calculus's real rail has NO trackId anywhere —
  <aside class="rail" id="rail"> (not "rail-calculus") and every onclick is the single-argument
  goChapter(id) (not goChapter(id, trackId)), unlike every other track. Root goChapter()'s trackId
  argument is itself optional (defaults to the current view) — calculus's source simply never
  passes it, likely a legacy artifact of it being the site's original/flagship track. Set true only
  for calculus.
#}
{% import "partials/_bilingual.njk" as bl %}
<aside class="rail"{% if not railNoTrackId %} id="rail-{{ trackId }}"{% else %} id="rail"{% endif %}>
  <p class="rt">{{ bl.text({"en": "Chapters", "ar": "الفصول"}) }}</p>
  {% for chapter in chapters %}
  {% if chapter.railGroupLabel %}<p class="rt" style="margin-top:16px">{{ chapter.railGroupLabel }}</p>{% endif %}
  <a data-target="{{ chapter.id }}" onclick="goChapter('{{ chapter.id }}'{% if not railNoTrackId %},'{{ trackId }}'{% endif %})"><span class="num">{{ chapter.chapterNumber }}</span>{{ bl.text(chapter.railLabel or chapter.title) }}</a>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if practiceSetId %}
  <a data-target="{{ practiceSetId }}" onclick="goChapter('{{ practiceSetId }}'{% if not railNoTrackId %},'{{ trackId }}'{% endif %})"><span class="num">{{ practiceSetIcon or '§' }}</span>{% if practiceSetLabel %}{{ practiceSetLabel }}{% else %}{{ bl.text({"en": "Practice set", "ar": "مجموعة تدريبية"}) }}{% endif %}</a>
  {% endif %}
  {% if testGeneratorId %}
  <a data-target="{{ testGeneratorId }}" onclick="goChapter('{{ testGeneratorId }}'{% if not railNoTrackId %},'{{ trackId }}'{% endif %})"><span class="num">✎</span>{{ bl.text({"en": "Test generator", "ar": "مولّد الاختبارات"}) }}</a>
  {% endif %}
  {% if downloadsId %}
  <a data-target="{{ downloadsId }}" onclick="goChapter('{{ downloadsId }}'{% if not railNoTrackId %},'{{ trackId }}'{% endif %})"><span class="num">↓</span>{{ bl.text({"en": "Downloads", "ar": "تنزيلات"}) }}</a>
  {% endif %}
  {% if railExtra %}{{ railExtra | safe }}{% endif %}
</aside>
